node_modules/
dist/

# `web/public/` is output of round one's web build, removed on 2026-09-27. A checkout that ever
# ran it still holds the generated wasm and its glue on disk, and nothing deletes an ignored file
# when its ignore goes — so it stays until no checkout has it.
web/public/

# The web app (the light app's `web` mode): `npm run web:wasm` writes the engine — wasm-bindgen's
# glue and the module — to `dist-wasm/`, and `npm run web:build` bundles the page into
# `apps/light/dist-web/` with a copy of it. `eslint.config.js` ignores both and `vite.watch.ts` keeps
# every dev server's watcher out of them.
apps/light/dist-web/
dist-wasm/

# The shared-collection viewer's bundle. `infrastructure/share-worker/wrangler.jsonc` declares an `assets`
# binding over it, so a deploy needs it on disk and nothing needs it in the history.
apps/share/dist-share/
apps/light/dist-mobile/
storybook-static/
# `apps/desktop/tsconfig.node.json` is `composite`, so anything that builds it as a *project* — `tsc -b`,
# or an editor's TS server doing the same — drops a `.tsbuildinfo` beside it. `npm run build`
# does not (plain `tsc` ignores `references`), which is why this arrives on a developer's
# machine and never in CI, and why it is worth a line rather than a diagnosis.
*.tsbuildinfo
# The cargo workspace's build tree, at the root where cargo puts it by default and where
# `.cargo/config.toml` pins it (the layout change of 2026-10-08 moved it from `src-tauri/target`).
# Anchored: it is the workspace's alone, and `crates/*/target/` below names the standalone crates'.
/target/
apps/desktop/src-tauri/data/
# `vitest run --coverage` writes here. The Rust side's equivalent lands under
# `target/llvm-cov/`, which the line above already covers.
coverage/
data/
*.local
.DS_Store
.superpowers/
# Claude Code parks git worktrees here: whole second checkouts of this repo. `git add -A`
# would otherwise try to embed one as a gitlink.
.claude/worktrees/
planned-features.txt

# design-sync (claude.ai/design). What is committed is the *input* to a sync — the config,
# the authored entry barrel and tsconfig, NOTES.md, conventions.md and any owned previews or
# adapter forks — because a re-sync replays every decision this repo has already made. What
# is ignored is everything a run regenerates: the staged converter and its deps, the emitted
# bundle, the reference storybook (minutes to build, megabytes, and derived from `packages/ui/`), and
# the per-run verification scratch. Verified state deliberately does NOT live in git: it
# travels in the uploaded project's own `_ds_sync.json`, which is what lets a sync from a
# second machine skip re-verifying what this one already proved.
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/sb-reference/
.design-sync/dist/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/.cache/
# Downloaded at sync time by `.design-sync/card-art.mjs`; card image bytes are never committed.
.design-sync/card-art/
.design-sync/node_modules
.design-sync/*.log
# Transient run logs. `npm run verify > verify.log` is the documented way to read a run
# (never pipe it), and one got committed by a `git add -A` before this rule existed.
*.log

# `wrangler`'s local working files under `infrastructure/relay/`, and the first of them is the one that matters.
# `.dev.vars` is wrangler's documented home for local secrets, which is exactly where
# `PATREON_CLIENT_SECRET` and `RELAY_HMAC_KEY` land the first time anyone runs `wrangler dev` —
# and this repo is public. `.wrangler/` is its local state directory (a miniflare D1 among other
# things); it already exists on disk. Both are ignored everywhere rather than only under
# `infrastructure/relay/`, because the habit here is `git add -A` and a secret only has to slip once.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.wrangler/

# An Android signing key, in every form `keytool` and a signing guide leave one in — the
# keystore, its base64 for `gh secret set`, and the properties file Tauri's signing guide has
# Gradle read. The release key lives in GitHub's secrets and in the owner's own backup, and is
# made **outside this folder** (docs/reference/ci-and-releases.md, "What only the owner can do");
# these lines are for the day it is made here anyway. This repo is public, and a lost key is
# every phone uninstalling — a leaked one is worse. And a signed bundle, should the owner
# download one into this folder on its way to Play Console.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore.b64
*.aab
keystore.properties
key.properties

# Transcripts from `tauri dev`, redirected so they can be grepped.
devlog*.txt

# The card scanner's standalone crate builds into its own target dir — it is not a member of
# a cargo workspace, so `/target/` above does not cover it.
crates/*/target/

# The frame bench's two modules — `npm run scanner:bench` runs `wasm-bindgen` into here, beside
# the page that loads them. (Everything else it builds, its invented inputs included, lands in
# `crates/card-scanner/target/`, which the line above covers.)
crates/card-scanner/bench/web/pkg/
# And a `target/` of the bench's own, which nothing makes today — its `.cargo/config.toml` and
# the script both name the scanner's — but `crates/*/target/` is one level short of, the day a
# `cargo build` is run there with that config out of reach.
crates/card-scanner/bench/target/

# Debug artifacts from `scan --debug-dir`. Regenerated by any run, ~50 MB per sweep.
.scanner-debug/

# Card-scanner reference bundle and its fetch cache. ~4.5 GB of source images reduced
# to a few MB; regenerated by `build-hashes`.
.scanner-bundle/

# The three scanner files `build.rs` embeds, downloaded by `npm run scanner:assets` from a
# GitHub release. The README stays tracked because it keeps the directory in existence, and a
# `rerun-if-changed` on a missing directory would rerun `build.rs` on every build.
apps/desktop/src-tauri/scanner-assets/*
!apps/desktop/src-tauri/scanner-assets/README.md

# A vitest JSON reporter's output, when a run asks for one.
.vitest/

# What a checkout that predates the layout change of 2026-10-08 still holds on disk: `src-tauri/`
# (the old build tree, `scanner-assets/`, `gen/schemas`), `mobile/` (`src-tauri/gen/schemas`) and
# the bundles that sat at the root (`dist-web/`, `dist-mobile/`, `dist-share/`; the root `dist/` is
# already covered by the unanchored line at the top). Nothing tracked lives in any of them any
# more, so without these lines a pull leaves them as untracked files for `git add -A` to stage.
# The owner deletes the folders once `src-tauri/target/debug/data` has moved to
# `target/debug/data`; this block can go when no checkout has them.
/src-tauri/
/mobile/
/dist-web/
/dist-mobile/
/dist-share/
